        ":question/id": "bd415fe2-3ead-5cbb-88ba-59d9d1273317",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-94740",
        ":question/problem": "Let $L$ be the set of all functions from $(0,\\infty )$ to $R$ of the form $f(x)=a{log}_{2}⁡(x),$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ is associative.\n- **II.** For any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$ and $f(x)\\in L,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n- **III.** For any $\\alpha \\in R$ and any $f(x),g(x)\\in L,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in (0,\\infty ),$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta f(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in (0,\\infty ),$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in (0,\\infty ),$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""
      },
